W H7, B D7, W H6, B J5, W J4, B H8, W J6, B J3, W D3, B C2, W D2, B B7 (C7 atari), W H2?, B G2,
W J8, B H9, W E1, B F1, W D1, B H1, W E3, B C1, W H5 (capture J5), B J9, W G8! (H8-H9-J9 had
2 libs; B F8 atari ignored), W G9 captures 3, B F9, W D8, B C8 (captures C7), W H8, B D9,
W E8?? (D8 libs miscounted: C7 is DIAGONAL to D8), B E9 captures 2, pass pass.
Final: my one big group (row 4 wall + right side) lived with eyes J5/J7/H9 = 30 pts. Black had
the top-left, the whole left and the whole bottom row 1-3 strip.
Takeaways:
- THE LOSS = THE OPENING SHAPE. vs tengen, W C4 / B C5 attach / W D4 / B D5 / W E4 / W F4...
  I crawled along the 4th line under Black's 5th-line wall. My wall then had Black above (row 5)
  AND Black invading below (G3, E2, C3, C2). A wall sandwiched between enemy stones has NO eye
  space: for 30 moves I was only fighting to live, never to score.
  => Never answer a "hane-on-head"/attach on top by extending along the same line 3+ times.
  => vs tengen as White: play low and make bases: 3-3/3-4 points in two DIFFERENT corners
     (e.g. C3 then G7, or C4 then G6) so each lives easily; don't build one long wall.
  => If I do have a 4th-line wall, the space BELOW it (rows 1-3) must be secured at once
     (e.g. D2/E2/G3 myself) before Black invades it. Black's G3+E2+C3 took all of it.
- Semeai/eye reading worked late: J4 killed J5 (black H5 would be suicide); G8 tesuji captured
  3 stones because H8-H9-J9 had 2 libs and black's F8 atari on G8 left G9 capturing.
- Liberty miscount again: D8's neighbours are C8/E8/D9/D7 — NOT C7. Use libs.py before
  every move in a fight, not just sometimes.

